Package: model3d
Version: @VERSION@
Architecture: amd64
Maintainer: Ronald Daniel Acuña Arias <ronald32acunadev@gmail.com>
Section: graphics
Priority: optional
Depends: python3, python3-pydantic, python3-pyside6.qtcore, python3-pyside6.qtgui, python3-pyside6.qtwidgets, python3-pyside6.qtnetwork, python3-pyside6.qtwebsockets, python3-pyside6.qtwebenginecore, python3-pyside6.qtwebenginewidgets, build-essential, patch
Homepage: https://github.com/ronald32acunadev/Model3dCreation
Description: Turn an image into a textured, optionally rigged 3D model on your own NVIDIA GPU
 Model3D generates GLB models locally with Hunyuan3D 2.1 and adds skeletons with UniRig.
 On first start its setup wizard checks the NVIDIA driver and CUDA toolkit 13, then
 installs the engine, its Python environment, and about 40 GB of models into a folder
 you choose. A Blender add-on is included in /opt/model3d/blender.
